  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<img height=\"138\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/11cd197a-69fa-47ca-8a3a-5a42213a905a-image.png\" width=\"210\" /></p>Compound (A)&nbsp;gives a white precipitate when warmed with alcoholic <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>means it contain a removable chloride&nbsp;atom(Benzylic position)<sub>.</sub>&nbsp;Oxidation of (A) gives an acid (B), <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>. (B) easily forms anhydride on heating. Means both acid should be ortho position of each other.<p><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f739a781-ac88-4863-8eac-590d7792d214-image.png\" style=\"width: 613px; height: 305px;\" /><br />&nbsp;</p>",
